insert into news (date_label,sort_date,category,title,body,tags,service_key,is_video,video_url,source_name,source_url,sources,status,office_key,image_url) values ('From about the 14th century','1300-01-01','History','The Marghi: Damboa’s first people','The first people of Damboa are the Marghi. Their own traditions say they came down from the Mandara mountains and the highlands of what is now northern Cameroon, moving not all at once but clan by clan – a clan is called a fal in Marghi. As the Borno kingdom grew stronger, many Marghi groups drifted further south, and by about the fourteenth century they were living on the open plains they still farm today.
insert into news (date_label,sort_date,category,title,body,tags,service_key,is_video,video_url,source_name,source_url,sources,status,office_key,image_url) values ('Long ago','1800-01-01','History','How the calabash made Damboa a meeting place','Long before roads and lorries, Damboa was known for one crop above others: the calabash. Grown on the farms around the town, dried and cleaned, the calabash became bowls, water carriers, ladles and food covers in homes across Borno. In northeastern Nigeria calabashes are also an art form, their golden-brown shells etched with fine patterns of animals, people and shapes.
insert into news (date_label,sort_date,category,title,body,tags,service_key,is_video,video_url,source_name,source_url,sources,status,office_key,image_url) values ('Traditional crafts','1900-01-01','History','Smiths and hunters of Damboa','Damboa’s farms and market were not its only fame. The town was also known for skilled smiths. Reporters writing about Damboa in 2014 noted that the town had a guild of craftsmen who made long guns for local hunters.
insert into news (date_label,sort_date,category,title,body,tags,service_key,is_video,video_url,source_name,source_url,sources,status,office_key,image_url) values ('1970s','1970-01-01','History','Sambisa: when Damboa’s forest drew safari visitors','Part of the great Sambisa Forest lies within Damboa. Its name comes from Sambisa village, on the border with Gwoza. The forest covers about 518 square kilometres, and in colonial times a Sambisa Game Reserve covered more than 2,200 square kilometres in its eastern part.
insert into news (date_label,sort_date,category,title,body,tags,service_key,is_video,video_url,source_name,source_url,sources,status,office_key,image_url) values ('3 February 1976','1976-02-03','History','Borno State and Damboa Local Government are born','On 3 February 1976 the military Head of State, General Murtala Mohammed, created seven new states, Borno among them, out of the old North-Eastern State. It was one of the most important days in Nigeria’s administrative history – and it came just ten days before he was killed in a failed coup. Group Captain Mustapha Amin became the first Governor of Borno State in March 1976.
insert into news (date_label,sort_date,category,title,body,tags,service_key,is_video,video_url,source_name,source_url,sources,status,office_key,image_url) values ('2014','2014-07-18','History','The hard year: Damboa under attack','2014 was the hardest year in Damboa’s modern history. In January insurgents attacked the army base in the town and were driven back. On 4 July they returned with a larger force and attacked the base and the police station, and many families fled.
insert into news (date_label,sort_date,category,title,body,tags,service_key,is_video,video_url,source_name,source_url,sources,status,office_key,image_url) values ('August 2014','2014-08-25','History','Troops retake Damboa','Weeks after the town fell, Nigerian troops pushed back into Damboa. By late August 2014 the insurgents had been driven out, and the flag they had raised over the town was pulled down.
insert into news (date_label,sort_date,category,title,body,tags,service_key,is_video,video_url,source_name,source_url,sources,status,office_key,image_url) values ('2015 onwards','2015-06-01','History','The road home','Return began with the road. As the military reopened the Maiduguri–Damboa–Biu highway, vehicles started to run again, at first under escort. The Damboa motor park filled with buses and lorries, carrying traders, farmers and families back to the town.
insert into news (date_label,sort_date,category,title,body,tags,service_key,is_video,video_url,source_name,source_url,sources,status,office_key,image_url) values ('6 September 2016','2016-09-06','History','Damboa market reopens after two years','On Tuesday 6 September 2016 the Damboa township market opened its gates again, two years after it was closed by the attacks of 2014. The caretaker chairman of the council, Alhaji Abu Hong, performed the reopening at a ceremony in Damboa, saying the market could reopen because peace had returned to the area.
insert into news (date_label,sort_date,category,title,body,tags,service_key,is_video,video_url,source_name,source_url,sources,status,office_key,image_url) values ('25 March 2024','2024-03-25','History','The Monday livestock market returns','On Monday 25 March 2024 the famous Damboa Monday Market – the livestock market – reopened, and buyers and sellers came from across Borno State and beyond.
